# Full CRM setup: docs/SUPABASE_CRM_SETUP.md
# Local: Docker + `npm run supabase:start` then `npm run supabase:status` → paste URL + keys below.

# Shared CRM password cookie: required for /admin when Supabase is NOT configured (preview/sample data).
# When Supabase IS configured, set this to require this password first, then Supabase email + password.
# CRM_SHARED_PASSWORD=your-strong-shared-secret

# Supabase Configuration
# Project URL: Settings → General (or top of API section) — https://xxxxx.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
# "Public" key — use EITHER the new Publishable key (sb_publishable_…) OR Legacy "anon" JWT (eyJ…)
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-or-anon-key-here
# "Backend" key — use EITHER the new Secret key (sb_secret_…) OR Legacy "service_role" JWT (eyJ…)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-secret-or-service-role-key-here

# MailerSend (already in use for room planner)
MAILERSEND_API_TOKEN=your-mailersend-token
MAILERSEND_FROM_EMAIL=team@playerstall.com
# CRM email templates: “Send as” Custom Sport Lockers uses this from-address (verify domain in MailerSend)
MAILERSEND_FROM_EMAIL_CUSTOM_SPORT_LOCKERS=sales@customsportslockers.com

# Optional: CRM “Client copy” page — override CSV URL (Google Sheets publish/export or any raw CSV URL)
# CLIENT_COPY_CSV_URL=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/YOUR_ID/export?format=csv&gid=0

# Bunny.net Edge Storage (optional — local scripts to list/upload/audit files on the CDN origin)
# Dashboard: Storage → your storage zone → FTP & API.
# HTTP header on every Storage API call: AccessKey: <one of the passwords below>
#
# Full “Password” (read/write) — use for scripts that upload, overwrite, or delete objects:
# BUNNY_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=your-storage-zone-password
#
# “Read-only password” (if enabled on the zone) — use for list/download-only tooling (audits, CI):
# BUNNY_STORAGE_READ_ONLY_KEY=your-read-only-password
# Omit read-only if you don’t use it; never put the full password in a read-only slot.
# Storage zone name = first path segment in the API URL (same name shown in the dashboard).
# BUNNY_STORAGE_ZONE_NAME=playerstall
# Host must be the Storage API hostname from Storage → your zone → FTP & API (same region as the zone).
# Do NOT use your CDN/pull hostname (e.g. *.b-cdn.net) here — that is not the Storage API.
# Examples: ny.storage.bunnycdn.com, la.storage.bunnycdn.com, storage.bunnycdn.com (Frankfurt), uk.storage.bunnycdn.com, sg.storage.bunnycdn.com, se.storage.bunnycdn.com, br.storage.bunnycdn.com, jh.storage.bunnycdn.com, syd.storage.bunnycdn.com
# BUNNY_STORAGE_HOST=ny.storage.bunnycdn.com

# Bunny.net account API (optional — pull zone purge, stats, etc.; NOT the storage zone password)
# Dashboard: Account → API → API key
# BUNNY_ACCOUNT_API_KEY=your-account-api-key
